post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
Google Drive for Omarchy Files is installed.

Connect an account:
  omarchy-gdrive-setup

Add more accounts from Files: right-click an empty area and choose
"Add Google Drive Account…" (needs nautilus-python).

Each account's My Drive is synced to ~/GoogleDrive/<email>: every file is
stored locally and saves are uploaded to Google Drive automatically.
Shared drives start online-only; right-click one in Files and choose
"Keep Everything on This Device" (or "Keep on This Device" on a folder)
to sync it.

Files loads extensions at startup, so restart it once after installing:
  nautilus --quit

The first run opens a browser for Google authorization and creates the
sync folder, the bookmark, and a systemd user service per account.

For reliable access, configure your own OAuth client:
  https://rclone.org/drive/#making-your-own-client-id
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  cat <<'EOF'
Google Drive for Omarchy keeps My Drive fully synced on this device.
Newly added Shared drives now start online-only (nothing downloaded) until
you choose "Keep Everything on This Device" or "Keep on This Device" on a
folder in Files. Shared drives that already sync keep syncing.

Upgrading from 0.4 or earlier (FUSE mounts)? Run the setup once:
  omarchy-gdrive-setup

Restart Files to load the new menu items:
  nautilus --quit
EOF
}

pre_remove() {
  cat <<'EOF'
Per-user data is not removed automatically:
  - ~/GoogleDrive/<email>            (one folder per account)
  - ~/.config/omarchy-gdrive/accounts.tsv
  - ~/.config/rclone/rclone.conf
  - ~/.config/systemd/user/rclone-*.service
  - the account email bookmarks in ~/.config/gtk-3.0/bookmarks
See /usr/share/doc/omarchy-gdrive/README.md for cleanup steps.
EOF
}
